  concept: 'Authored objective: Qualify Dynamic Stability.

    Authored requirement:
    Voltage ripple, transients, efficiency and protection tests

    General teaching
    principle: Electrical measurements are differences or flows that require a correct
    reference, operating condition and fresh solver evidence.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
